/*
  THE PROOF SCRIPTS WERE NOT TYPECHECKED BY ANYTHING.

  `tsconfig.json` includes `src` only and `tsconfig.node.json` names three
  files, so every script under `scripts/` — the acceptance tests this repo
  leans on, the ones `npm test` runs — compiled nowhere. They run under `tsx`,
  which strips types without checking them.

  That is the safety net having no net. Found while adding a sixth field to
  `SymbolSetup`: the compiler named every place in `src` that had to change,
  and said nothing about the proof fixture that constructs one — so the proof
  went on passing while writing `priceScale: undefined` into the record it was
  asserting round-trips losslessly.

  Extends the app config (same `strict`, same DOM lib — the proofs import real
  components) and adds `src` so project references are resolved the same way
  the app resolves them. `types: ["node"]` for `process.exit`, which the proofs
  use to fail a build.
*/
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts", "src"],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["node"]
  }
}
